ose in the same direction more often than not GBP/USD runs into resistance at last week's low \u8226\'20\'22 Cable met headwind at 1.2163 after extending north from 1.2109 (Asia low) \u8226\'20\'22 1.2163 is ex-support point (last week's low). Sub-1.2163 stops hit Wednesday \u8226\'20\'22 UK Q1 C/A deficit GBP 51.7 bln vs 39.8 bln f/c; \uc2 ONS\uc2  urges caution on data \u8226\'20\'22 Asia low was 3.5 pips shy of Wednesday's 13-day low \u8226\'20\'22 Weds low plumbed on hawkish Powell/dovish Dhingra \u8226\'20\'22 1.2291 was Tuesday's high -- before month-end buying of USD AUD/USD holds below 0.69 before U.S. core PCE data \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD has traded 23 pip range since 0600 GMT; 0.6873-0.6896 \u8226\'20\'22 Those parameters are within the 0.6854-0.6904 Asian session range \u8226\'20\'22 0.6854 marks the lowest level since June 14 \u8226\'20\'22 0.6850 was June 14 low (0.6829 was last month's low, May 12) \u8226\'20\'22 On Wednesday, Fed's Powell said clock is running to bring inflation down \u8226\'20\'22 U.S. May core PCE data due 1230 GMT; 4.8% YY f/c Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set EUR/USD free For more than a decade the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted by \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's National Bank has suppressed volatility, helping to contain EUR/USD in tighter ranges. That policy has ended now, and with it EUR/USD is free to move. It is prudent to expect bigger movement and greater volatility. When the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  it supports EUR/CHF underpinning EUR/USD too. When reserves are subsequently rebalanced with over 60% of the euros purchased sold and 39% converted to dollars it weighs EUR/USD. This has a top and tailing effect with EUR/USD supported at the outset and subsequently weighed, and because of the great size of SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  which saw reserves top 1 trillion Swiss francs, the SNB's made a big impression on EUR/USD curtailing volatility and almost certainly suppressed speculation. The intensification of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and doubling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves after the 1.2000 EUR/CHF peg was abandoned amplified the SNB's influence on EUR/USD with volatility sinking to a record low. Freed of the SNB and losing the enormous liquidity it provided EUR/USD can move more, and traders who have grown used to years of relative inactivity should anticipate greater movement. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3Ny37Lx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  Will BoE hike 50 bps before hawk flies GBP nest? Relatively dovish comments from incoming Bank of England Monetary Policy Committee member Swati Dhingra have upped the ante for sterling ahead of the next \uc2 BoE\uc2  rate decision on Aug. 4 -- when a 25 or 50 basis-point rate rise is expected. Dhingra on Wednesday said she favours "very gradual" moves on rates, which suggests she will not follow in the footsteps of hawk Michael Saunders, who she replaces on the MPC five days after August's rate verdict, in voting for 50 bps hikes. Assuming Saunders, Catherine Mann and Jonathan Haskel vote for a half-point hike on Aug. 4, and doves \uc2 Silvana Tenreyro\uc2  and Jon Cunliffe vote for a quarter-point increase, the crucial swing votes will be cast by Andrew Bailey, \uc2 Huw Pill\uc2 , Ben Broadbent and Dave Ramsden (who wanted to raise rates by 50 bps in February, before Russia invaded Ukraine). GBP/USD fell to a 13-day low just shy of 1.2100 in the wake of Dhingra's testimony on Wednesday. To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-3T11:14:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220630ei6u0238d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
