\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ- COMMENT-Switzerland's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  has set EUR/USD free\b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2022\par 10:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 June 30 (Reuters) - For more than a decade the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted by \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's National Bank has suppressed volatility, helping to contain EUR/USD in tighter ranges. That policy has ended now, and with it EUR/USD is free to move. It is prudent to expect bigger movement and greater volatility.\par \par \uc2 When the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  it supports EUR/CHF underpinning EUR/USD too. When reserves are subsequently rebalanced with over 60% of the euros purchased sold and 39% converted to dollars it weighs EUR/USD.\par \par \uc2 This has a top and tailing effect with EUR/USD supported at the outset and subsequently weighed, and because of the great size of SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  which saw reserves top 1 trillion Swiss francs, the SNB's made a big impression on EUR/USD curtailing volatility and almost certainly suppressed speculation.\par \par \uc2 The intensification of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and doubling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves after the 1.2000 EUR/CHF peg was abandoned amplified the SNB's influence on EUR/USD with volatility sinking to a record low.\par \par \uc2 Freed of the SNB and losing the enormous liquidity it provided EUR/USD can move more, and traders who have grown used to years of relative inactivity should anticipate greater movement.\par \par \uc2 For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Jeremy Boulton is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-3T08:15:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument 