\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-SNB's withdrawal should boost EUR/USD volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2021\par 12:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nov 3 (Reuters) - It appears that \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is curtailing a decade long \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  programme which should free up EUR/USD, lessening liquidity and boosting volatility.\par \par \uc2 Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a top and tailing affect upon EUR/USD - supporting the pair initially then weighing during rebalancing of reserves.\par \par \uc2 Given a lack of liquidity, buying EUR/CHF usually meant buying both cross and via the legs (EUR/USD and USD/CHF) which worked because the SNB had abundant lines of credit with local banks that saw the vast bulk of CHF flows.\par \par \uc2 This has underpinned EUR/USD for over 10 years but because 38% of reserves are held in dollars, a big part of EUR/CHF purchased saw SNB later selling EUR/USD. This was usually well timed with SNB selling ahead major levels and doing so when liquidity was heightened by speculative buying.\par \par \uc2 The result was that rebalancing often unexpectedly capped EUR/USD forcing traders to pare bets with vols subsequently falling.\par \par \uc2 Without the SNB's billions EUR/USD could get a lot more exciting\par \par \uc2 Related\par \par \uc2 For more click on (Jeremy Boulton is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-11-6T11:50:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211103ehb3028eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
