\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-GRAPHIC-Swiss franc moves higher as \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  report looms\b0\par\par\uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2021\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story published on Wednesday with no changes to text)\par \par \uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee and John Revill\par \par \uc2 LONDON/ZURICH, Oct 27 (Reuters) - The Swiss franc, at 11-month highs against the euro, looks set for further gains on back of higher inflation, hedge-fund positioning against market turbulence and above all, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has become far more tolerant of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.\par \par \uc2 The rise comes at an opportune time, just as the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  prepares to issue its report on trading partners' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. Its April report deemed Switzerland to meet the criteria to be named a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, though it stopped short of labelling it so.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 , has sharply scaled back \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tamp down the franc, even though it stands 4.6% firmer than the 18-month lows hit in early-2021 versus the euro .\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar it is near six-week highs, having firmed 3% since early-April.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Gallo\uc2 , head of European \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at BMO, says many speculators remain "long" Swiss franc against the dollar and euro "because they're concerned there will be some kind of a flare up in markets and as a result, they are buying upward exposure on the Swiss franc."\par \par \uc2 But while the franc, alongside other safe-haven assets such as gold and the yen, is monitored as a barometer of global markets' mood, most analysts reckon franc strength is no longer solely down to safety-seeking flows.\par \par \uc2 Below are five charts showing what's driving franc gains:\par \par \uc2 1/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Despite the franc's 2.6% rise versus the euro since mid-September, the SNB has largely steered clear of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stepping in recently for the first time in six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Stucki, chief investment officer at \uc2 St Galler Kantonalbank\uc2  and the former head of asset management at the SNB, reckons policymakers will retain their hands-off approach.\par \par \uc2 One reason is that expectations of interest rate rises from other central banks, such as the Fed and the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  may limit franc upward pressure.\par \par \uc2 "The franc's level is currently not a problem for the SNB and though the franc is strong, we don't have deflationary pressure," he said.\par \par \uc2 Swiss inflation is running at a two-year high of 0.94% in September.\par \par \uc2 2/DISAPPEARING DIFFERENTIALS\par \par \uc2 Franc appreciation bets are also being fanned by the expectation that higher inflation could elicit an interest rate rise from the SNB, said GianLuigi Mandruzatto, an economist at EFG Bank.\par \par \uc2 Unlike peers such as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Fed, the SNB has not tweaked its policy framework to introduce a higher inflation tolerance threshold. That implies it would need to act if inflation accelerates above its price stability target \u8211\'20\'13 defined as just below 2%.\par \par \uc2 Money markets are pricing a 15 basis-point rate rise from the SNB by end-2022, more than what is expected from the \uc2 ECB\uc2 . At -0.75% Swiss rates are the lowest in the world.\par \par \uc2 "By mid to end-2025, markets expect the current differential will be inverted, with interest rates 40 basis points higher in Switzerland than in the eurozone," Mandruzatto said.\par \par \uc2 "This 65 basis point differential is enormous in a world where interest rates are 0.01%. People will be buying into the franc now to benefit from this trend in the future." \par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par 3/ TRADE WEIGHTED FRANC\par               \par Against trade partners' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the franc no longer\par looks as overvalued as before versus long-term averages.\par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ING strategists believe while Switzerland ticks the boxes for being named as a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator by the Treasury, it may again dodge being labelled so.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The criteria include having a trade and current account surplus against the United States and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Switzerland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a $11.5 billion current account surplus with the United States in the June quarter, slightly down from March. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par 4/ DERIVATIVES\par               \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivative markets show little evidence that\par traders are betting big on any franc downside.\par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Implied volatility gauges on euro-franc are low and a few strikes strewn around the 1.02 to 1.05 francs per euro level indicate traders expect more gains for the franc. Strikes are levels around which traders put large bets in case the exchange rate hits that level. On Wednesday, the exchange rate was at 1.0628 franc per euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comparatively, hedge funds had large short bets in the futures markets suggesting any more franc gains can force some of these positions to be unwound causing more gains for the franc. \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Saikat Chatterjee in London and John Revill in Zurich; Additional reporting by Elizabeth Howcroft in London; Editing by Sujata Rao and Shailesh Kuber) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-10-28T07:00:02.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211028ehas0131t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
