ders are far better positioned for the drop than seemed likely \u8226\'20\'22 Close below 200-WMA 1.1575 and weekly cloud base 1.1538 may force change \u8226\'20\'22 Fri's close key, profit taking often precedes weekends, lessens risk break USD/JPY on course for the biggest monthly rise since March \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY sees big rise, it is currently up over 180 pips on the month \u8226\'20\'22 Yen set for worst month since March, Fed tightening in focus \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY has risen to hit new 2021 highs on Thursday on the EBS \u8226\'20\'22 Spot sees a 111.80-112.06 range so far Thursday, but heavy above 112.00 \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY chart brings the 2020 and 2019 highs into view \u8226\'20\'22 However, Japanese exporter offers could limit upside in the near-term \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY 30/60-day log correlations are both well above +0.50 GBP/USD up half-a-cent after threatening nine-month low \u8226\'20\'22 1.3469 is high water-mark for cable since its European am drop to 1.3417 \u8226\'20\'22 Rise to 1.3469 aided by some profit-taking on short GBP positions \u8226\'20\'22 1.3417 was five pips shy of Wednesday's nine-month low \u8226\'20\'22 Tuesday's high was 1.3717 -- before UK stagflation fears hurt the pound \u8226\'20\'22 UK economy bounced back by more than thought in Q2 before slowdown \u8226\'20\'22 Offers expected pre-1.35 if GBP/USD extends north AUD/USD 0.7220 flips to resistance after drop to 5-week low \u8226\'20\'22 Offers ahead of 0.7220 (former support point) are keeping a lid on AUD/USD \u8226\'20\'22 Momentum funds reportedly sold on Wednesday's break below 0.7220 \u8226\'20\'22 Bids pre-0.7220 propped AUD/USD last week (Sept 20-23) and on Tuesday \u8226\'20\'22 0.7171 was Wednesday's five-week low. Big 0.7200 option expiry today \u8226\'20\'22 Even bigger 0.7200 expiry Friday, A$1.7 billion strike \u8226\'20\'22 Dalian iron ore closed up 5.4% after scaling three-week peak \uc2 ECB\uc2  and SNB could be on a collision course over \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be on a collision course over Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to materially influence the value of the franc which it still deems too high means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells a lot of francs. Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose over 14 billion francs in August to almost one trillion francs and it is the subsequent rebalancing of the reserves that may become a problem. Thirty eight percent of Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are dollars. Of the 178 billion francs sold since March 2020 some 67 billion should have been sold to buy dollars. That is a huge weight on EUR/USD which is a problem for the euro zone's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that hopes to maintain easy policy in the face of rising inflation. By \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on such a grand scale, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  is making the \uc2 ECB\uc2 's task much harder, lessening the chance of the inflation rise proving temporary. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3mhIrfc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3mhIrfc}}}\uc2  Dollar could be on the verge of a bigger surge Month-end flows into the U.S. dollar have put it on the brink of breaking above a major Fibonacci level, above which it could accelerate further. Fundamental and technical factors combine to add to the underlying bullish market structure of the greenback. The dollar hovered near its highest levels in a year against a basket of peers on Thursday on rising expectations the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will taper stimulus from November. The USD index, which tracks the dollar against six \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has hit new 2021 highs, and is now focused on the major 94.471 Fibonacci level, a 38.2% retrace of the 102.99 to 89.206 (2020 to 2021) drop. The medium-term technical chart is reinforcing the underlying bullish market structure, 14-week momentum has been positive for 11 weeks in a row. Above the 94.471 Fibo would unmask the September 2020 94.745 peak for a retest initially. However, a failure to overcome the 94.471 could lead to a reversal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/39SY1rz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/39SY1rz}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3mdGtfK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3mdGtfK}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-10-3T10:48:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210930eh9u01yg5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
