\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-Swiss franc may be central to coming  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  movement\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2021\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Aug 24 (Reuters) - The Swiss franc is on the cusp of big levels which, if broken, should send shockwaves across broader \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and if these levels are to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which will also create waves. So the franc may be central to coming \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements.\par \par \uc2 It is rallying when it should be falling, like other funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have been undermined by stimulus that's boosting stocks and commodities and the low volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that undermines such negative-yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Instead, counter to Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, the franc is rising and has done so since March when Swiss reserves hit 1 trillion dollars.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has talked the franc down, but there's no real evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with reserves dropping and sight deposits unchanged this year.\par \par \uc2 If SNB stops \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , EUR/CHF may drop rapidly towards 2015's 1.0505, perhaps much lower. If not, the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that's now required could have a bigger than usual impact on currently quiet markets.\par \par \uc2 For more click on FXBUZ\par \par \uc2 (Jeremy Boulton is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed 