\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland \highlight\uc2 's SNB still ready for  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  as U.S. drops manipulator tag\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2021\par 17:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, background, further SNB comment)\par \par \uc2 By John Revill\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, April 16 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) said on Friday it remained ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, after the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  dropped its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator label for the country even though it met criteria for the designation.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  did not use the term \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in a new report, adding its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases were not intended to alter Swiss balance of payments or unfairly help the Swiss economy.\par \par \uc2 "The SNB's position is therefore clear: Switzerland does not engage in any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation," the SNB said.\par \par \uc2 In December, President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's outgoing administration labeled Switzerland and Vietnam manipulators.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury Department, now under President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in its latest report said it will undertake "enhanced engagement" with both countries as well as Taiwan, on grounds they met the criteria under a 2015 U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation law.\par \par \uc2 Still, a Treasury official said it was possible for countries like Switzerland to meet the tests under the 2015 law without being manipulators.\par \par \uc2 The report also concluded there was insufficient evidence under a separate 1988 law to conclude the three countries were manipulating exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 The SNB spent nearly 110 billion Swiss francs ($120 billion)on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2020, while the country ran a goods trade surplus of 28 billion Swiss francs with the United States, according to Swiss customs data.\par \par \uc2 While pledging to continue talks with Washington, the SNB said it would not change course from its ultra-expansive monetary policy, based on the world's lowest interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The SNB's monetary policy approach...remains unchanged," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. "In view of the economic situation and the ongoing high value of the Swiss franc, the SNB remains ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary."\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 0.9190 Swiss francs) (Reporting by John Revill, editing by John Miller) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-4-16T16:15:15.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210416eh4g02vbi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
