\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Swiss cenbank to press ahead with  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  despite U.S. manipulation tag\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2020\par 15:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds government comment)\par \par \uc2 By John Revill\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, Dec 16 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  rejected accusations of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation by the United States on Wednesday, saying the label would not deter it from acting aggressively on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  had earlier said \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Vietnam were \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators that had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to devalue their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar and prevent effective balance of payments adjustments.\par \par \uc2 "The SNB's monetary policy approach remains unchanged by the report," the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. "In light of the economic situation and the fact that the Swiss franc is still highly valued, the SNB remains willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more strongly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 It added that its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not intended to gain unfair trading advantage for Swiss exporters or massage balance of payments figures. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are necessary in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy to ensure appropriate monetary conditions and therefore price stability," the SNB said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, spending 90 billion Swiss francs ($101.72 billion) in the first half to rein in the franc, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has argued this is to prevent the "highly valued" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from triggering deflation.\par \par \uc2 Officials from the Swiss government and the SNB are in contact with U.S. counterparts to explain the situation, the SNB added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to give its latest monetary policy update on Thursday, where it is expected to reiterate its commitment to negative interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Swiss government noted the report, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not manipulate the Swiss franc or seek to gain any unfair advantage for its economy.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the State Secretariat for International Finance said the country was open to bilateral talks with Washington on the matter.\par \par \uc2 "Switzerland is confident that the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  will carefully analyse the country's situation, taking due account of the specific characteristics of Switzerland and the Swiss economy," she said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 0.8848 Swiss francs) (Reporting by John Revill; Editing by Michael Shields and Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-16T15:58:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201216egcg02gi5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
