\par\par \b \uc2 Hedge funds test Swiss tolerance with franc gambit\b0\par\par\uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2020\par 07:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Franc hits 4-1/2-year high vs euro\par \par \uc2 * U.S. in Jan added \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchlist\par \par \uc2 * Some say SNB will eventually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hitting franc\par \par \uc2 * Euro/franc at 1.05 seen as red line for SNB\par \par \uc2 By Tommy Wilkes\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Hedge funds betting that the Swiss franc will climb further against the euro will soon meet their match, according to investors who are taking the other side of the trade.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday climbed to a 4-1/2 year high of 1.061 francs per euro, fast approaching the point where its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will feel compelled to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength does not harm the country's export-dependent economy, these investors argue.\par \par \uc2 A catalyst was Switzerland's inclusion last month into a \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  watchlist for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation, which led many to bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take a more hands-off approach to the franc.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about the euro zone economy have also contributed significantly to franc gains versus the euro, handing a 2%-plus profit to hedge funds that piled into the franc and sold the euro a month back.\par \par \uc2 But many reckon the SNB remains too concerned about franc strength pressuring inflation and exports to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether.\par \par \uc2 "We think the move downward (in the euro/franc exchange rate) has been overdone," said Van Luu, Head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income Strategy at \uc2 Russell Investments\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Luu said the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  would "continue to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it has explicitly stated its role in monetary policymaking," adding that the franc was the most shorted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its $5.6 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund.\par \par \uc2 According to some measures the franc is now at least 4% overvalued. Yet speculators' net long position on the franc versus the dollar has swelled to the biggest since late-2016 .\par \par \uc2 These positions are at risk of a shakeout if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  suddenly.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, hedge funds have focused on buying the franc and selling the euro on spot markets, often magnifying their bets with leverage. Option traders said volatility on euro/franc derivatives markets was low and trading volumes very thin.\par \par \uc2 What would it take to force the SNB's hand?\par \par \uc2 Ian Gunner\uc2 , portfolio manager at hedge fund Altana Wealth, said headlines about franc strength was "the last thing the SNB wants to see.\par \par \uc2 "I'm looking for a sign that we have bottomed against the euro," he said, pointing to 1.05 francs as the level beyond which the SNB would have to act.\par \par \uc2 Investors interviewed for this article generally saw 1.05 francs per euro - just 1% from current levels - as the threshold.\par \par \uc2 Andreas Koenig, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Amundi Asset Management\uc2 , said the threshold had shifted from a range of 1.10-1.08 francs per euro before the watchlist was released to 1.08-1.06 francs today, a band it is close to breaching.\par \par \uc2 NOT SO STRONG\par \par \uc2 Still, the SNB may not be panicking just yet.\par \par \uc2 Despite the franc's gains versus the euro and outperformance compared to another safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen versus the dollar, its showing more broadly is less impressive even with safe-haven flows driven by China's coronavirus outbreak.\par \par \uc2 The franc is down 1% versus the dollar so far in 2020 .\par \par \uc2 And while the trade-weighed franc index has climbed, it is well off 2017 highs when the SNB called the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  'significantly overvalued'.\par \par \uc2 The SNB denies its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aim to give \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  a trading advantage, instead noting the impact a highly-valued franc has on inflation.\par \par \uc2 But the symbolism of appearing on the watchlist may have taken on new meaning under U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's a new environment. These are not empty threats. They (the U.S.) will follow through," said Stephen Jen, hedge fund manager at Eurizon SLJ Capital, describing the political capacity of \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as "compromised".\par \par \uc2 Recent sight deposit data, a gauge of Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity, indeed suggests the SNB has not been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly.\par \par \uc2 The bank is - at least verbally - sticking to its guns. Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  said last week the SNB would still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Amundi's Koenig is positioning for "tactical recovery" in euro/franc.\par \par \uc2 "The market thinks the SNB cannot do anything anymore. But the SNB is not at the end of its possibilities."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tommy Reggiori Wilkes Additional reporting by Saikat Chatterjee in London and John Revill in Zurich Editing by Sujata Rao)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-17T06:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200214eg2e00lzp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
