\par\par \b \uc2 SNB not beggaring neigbours by reining in franc - Jordan\b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2017\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BASEL, Nov 23 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's massive foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases to weaken the Swiss franc are not a deliberate 'beggar-thy-neighbour' approach to gain unfair advantage at the expense of Switzerland's trade partners, SNB Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling francs for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in vast amounts for years to keep a lid on the soaring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose rise has spelt danger for \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- which have inflated the SNB's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings to 742 billion Swiss francs ($747.76 billion) -- have attracted the attention of the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  looking to crack down on international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland's current account surplus of around 10 percent of GDP - the seventh-largest surplus in the world - was another cause for concern for U.S. officials, who put Switzerland on a watch list along with China, Japan, South Korea and Germany.\par \par \uc2 Jordan said the SNB had to be active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets because reducing interest rates was not enough to steer monetary policy in the current low-rate environment.\par \par \uc2 "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not amount to a mercantilist policy at the expense of Switzerland's trading partners or a beggar-thy-neighbour strategy," Jordan said in remarks prepared for a conference in Basel on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Rather, this policy provides the SNB with a necessary instrument for ensuring price stability and for fulfilling its mandate."\par \par \uc2 Switzerland has been on the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's monitoring list since 2016 and appeared again in October on the list which aims to curb what the U.S. calls "unfair \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices".\par \par \uc2 Switzerland met two of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation criteria -- having a material current account surplus at 10.3 percent of GDP and having engaged in a "sizeable one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases", the U.S. report said.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland's $6.6 billion first-half bilateral trade surplus with the United States fell short of the third criteria, which could have triggered bilateral talks aimed at correcting the situation.\par \par \uc2 "We are maintaining a constructive dialogue on this matter with the responsible government agencies in the U.S.," Jordan said.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland's high current account surplus was not due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, but to special factors like the country's ageing population and strong presence of merchanting and pharmaceuticals companies which were less affected by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 Despite a slight weakening of the franc, Jordan described the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as "remaining highly valued." (Reporting by John Revill; Editing by Michael Shields)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-11-26T16:30:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171123edbn00nax\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
