\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -US dollar bounces back, bolstered by solid U.S. data\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2017\par 16:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * U.S. dollar rises vs euro, yen\par \par \uc2 * Dollar up more than 1.0 pct vs Swiss franc\par \par \uc2 * Graphic: World \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in 2017 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2  (Updates to U.S. trading, new throughout, changes dateline, previous LONDON)\par \par \uc2 By Dion Rabouin\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, July 27 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar rallied against the euro and yen on Thursday after solid U.S. economic data, bouncing back from lows plumbed after Wednesday's \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  monetary policy statement.\par \par \uc2 U.S. durable goods orders rose more than expected last month and a fifth straight monthly increase in shipments suggested that business spending on equipment would support economic growth in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 The good durable goods orders data was a welcome sign to dollar bulls, as U.S. economic data, including subdued inflation, and uncertainty surrounding U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's proposed fiscal stimulus have sunk the dollar in recent months.\par \par \uc2 The euro on Thursday fell 0.5 percent against the dollar, slipping back below the $1.17 mark.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 0.3 percent against the yen to 111.50 yen.\par \par \uc2 "The most significant thing was the durable goods orders, those came in much better than expected," said Sireen Harajli, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2 . "Especially given that the recent data releases in the U.S. have been coming in on the weaker side, I think that was welcome news this morning."\par \par \uc2 The dollar sank on Wednesday after the Fed's policy statement remained largely unchanged from June and suggested the Fed was in no hurry to raise interest rates again.\par \par \uc2 Soft U.S. data on inflation and consumer spending so far this year have pushed the dollar to multi-year lows against the euro, which has also been underpinned by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's talk of reducing its ultra-loose monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The euro has risen more than 11 percent against the dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 "The euro's seven-month surge ... to near the top of its three-year $1.0341-$1.1714 range has called into question our expectations for the pair to range-trade through year-end," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said in a forecast update.\par \par \uc2 "(But) we continue to believe that the conditions for a euro breakout are not yet met."\par \par \uc2 Analysts also said investigations into the Trump administration's ties to Russia, and the inability of Trump's fellow Republicans to push through the president's promised repeal of the 2010 Affordable Care Act, have reduced the likelihood of tax reform and infrastructure spending plans being enacted soon also.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc was the biggest mover among major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , falling to its weakest since the collapse of an official cap in 2015.\par \par \uc2 The franc has held largely steady for the past two years as a result of capital seeking the security of \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a campaign of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Thursday the dollar rose 1.3 percent against the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 0.9618 franc.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Dion Rabouin; Additional reporting by Patrick Graham and Sujata Rao-Coverley in London) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-7-27T15:59:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170727ed7r00lor\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
