\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Swiss franc hits lowest since 2015 cap shock, dollar steadies\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2017\par 12:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts following Swiss franc move)               \par \par \uc2 * Graphic: World \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in 2017 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\par \par \uc2 By Patrick Graham               \par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 27 (Reuters) - The Swiss franc's fall to its weakest since the collapse of an official cap in 2015 dominated major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Thursday, and the dollar recovered from a fall to 2-1/2 year lows.               \par \par \uc2 The franc, held largely steady for the past two years between capital seeking the security of \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a campaign of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had already fallen almost 2 percent this week.               \par \par \uc2 It sank by as much as another 1 percent against the dollar and the euro in morning trade in Europe, while other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs were broadly steady.               \par \par \uc2 "The safe haven trade for the Swiss franc is starting to unwind," said Michael Hewson, chief markets strategist at \uc2 CMC Markets\uc2  in London.               \par \par \uc2 By 1020 GMT, the franc had steadied a little to trade 0.6 percent weaker at 1.1231 francs per euro. It lost 0.9 percent to 0.9587 francs per dollar.               \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the main trigger was the change in the outlook for global monetary policy, which has seen expectations of tighter financial conditions - and relatively higher market interest rates - in the euro zone grow.               \par \par \uc2 "Upside pressure on the franc will diminish as we see higher euro rates," said Commerzbank analyst Antje Praefcke.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  drove the dollar lower on Wednesday with a policy statement that stuck to its promises on tightening but mentioned weakness in U.S. inflation more explicitly than before.               \par \par \uc2 That played into doubts among international investors over U.S. economic growth and extended a sporadic slide for the dollar index that dates back to early March.               \par \par \uc2 Against the euro, it has fallen 13 percent from a peak hit in January, and 5 percent in the past four weeks, stirring concerns over how much more euro strength \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers will be willing to allow without reacting.               \par \par \uc2 By late morning in Europe, the dollar had gained 0.2 percent on the day at $1.1713 per euro, having hit a low of $1.1777 in Asian trading.               \par \par \uc2 "The euro's seven-month surge ... to near the top of its three-year $1.0341-$1.1714 range has called into question our expectations for the pair to range-trade through year-end," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said in a forecast update.               \par \par \uc2 "(But) we continue to believe that the conditions for a euro breakout are not yet met."               \par \par \uc2 For Reuters Live Markets blog on European and UK stock markets see reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url={\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://emea1.apps.cp.extranet.thomsonreuters.biz/cms/?pageId=livemarkets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://emea1.apps.cp.extranet.thomsonreuters.biz/cms/?pageId=livemarkets}}}\par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-7-27T11:39:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170727ed7r00ei0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
