\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Ready To Curb Franc Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2016\par 14:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH\u8212\'20\'14The Swiss franc remains "considerably overvalued," with \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary, a top Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Despite the franc's strength Swiss companies remain highly competitive due to investments in research and development and a highly-skilled workforce, said Swiss National Bank Vice Chairman Fritz Zurbr\u252\'00\'FC gg.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Zurbr\u252\'00\'FC gg's prepared comments of a speech to Swiss business leaders came nearly one year after the SNB shook global financial markets by abandoning a ceiling it had set for more than three years on the Swiss franc's value against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The move, last Jan. 15, led to a sharp rise in the franc and made Swiss products more expensive in global markets while contributing to falling consumer prices at home. The euro fetched 1.09 francs midday in Europe Wednesday. The franc is worth about 10% more against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than it was when the SNB enforced the 1.20 ceiling.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Zurbr\u252\'00\'FC gg said he was "convinced that the SNB's decision came at the right time.\par \par \uc2 "Without this difficult step, we would have compromised our ability to fulfill our mandate of ensuring price stability in the medium and long term," he said. The franc ceiling had become unsustainable and costly to enforce, he said, echoing other remarks by SNB officials.\par \par \uc2 "Swiss competitiveness came under pressure in the short term," Mr. Zurbr\u252\'00\'FC gg said. "Yet Switzerland's position among the leaders in major international rankings clearly shows that, over the long term, exchange-rate developments are only one factor shaping competitiveness."\par \par \uc2 The SNB last year reduced the rate it sets on certain bank deposits parked at the SNB to -0.75% to weaken the attractiveness of Swiss assets. Officials have said they are willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 "These measures demonstrate that business as usual is still a long way off," Mr. Zurbr\u252\'00\'FC gg said. "During the crises of the last few years, recurring safe-haven flows of both domestic and foreign capital have led to severe upward pressure on the Swiss franc. Despite weakening somewhat over recent months, the franc is still considerably overvalued."\par \par \uc2 He pegged the present overvaluation at about 15% based on the franc's long-term average exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brian Blackstone at brian.blackstone@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 13, 2016 08:45 ET (13:45 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160113ec1d001td\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
