\par\par \b \uc2 Euro satellites caught in \uc2 ECB\uc2  slipstream, risk policy errors\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2015\par 16:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  balance sheets since 2007 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/ged46s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/ged46s}}}\par \par \uc2 By Dhara Ranasinghe and Anirban Nag\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Aggressive monetary easing by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week might well be needed in the euro zone, but it's dragging neighbouring countries into even more extreme and unprecedented steps to stop their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthening against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers from Stockholm to Zurich are widely expected to be drawn into further dramatic domestic easing to match Thursday's \uc2 ECB\uc2  action. Outside the 19-nation bloc, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressures leave them with little option and some are fearful they are being drawn into policy mistakes.\par \par \uc2 "All the smaller central banks in Europe - Sweden, Denmark, Switzerland - are essentially in the gravity field of \uc2 the ECB\uc2 ," said Reinhard Cluse, chief economist for Europe at UBS.\par \par \uc2 Just as euro zone money markets are pricing in \uc2 ECB\uc2  interest rate cuts on Thursday, Swiss equivalents also reflect the possibility of easier policy to come.\par \par \uc2 The three-month Swiss Libor rate has shed 10 basis points since the start of November and at around -0.85 percent is below the -0.75 percent deposit rate and veering towards the lower end of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's -0.25 to -1.25 percent target range, as this graphic shows: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/1NHlU6H"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/1NHlU6H}}}\par \par \uc2 Swiss two-year government bond yields touched a record low -1.214 percent on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The SNB abandoned its cap on the franc's exchange rate against the euro in January because, with \uc2 the ECB\uc2  in easing mode, it was difficult to keep the franc steady.\par \par \uc2 With a combination of negative interest rates and SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, the franc has dropped to a near two-month low against the euro and a five-year trough against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Traders expect the SNB to ramp up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, the SNB still describes the franc as "significantly overvalued" and Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  told a newspaper last week the SNB had no limit on increasing its balance sheet, compared in this graphic. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/ged46s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/ged46s}}}\par \par \uc2 But such measures will come at a cost, with many in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  opposed to the SNB expanding its balance sheet through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it already stands at 80 percent of gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 NO SENSE\par \par \uc2 In Sweden, markets have also begun to anticipate rate cuts in the months ahead, a move that some say makes no sense in an economy growing at almost four percent year on year and where low rates are stoking a housing bubble {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyw74w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyw74w}}}\par \par \uc2 "We all know rates don't have to be bumped too much higher for it to pinch the household sector," said Richard Falkenhall, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at SEB, a large \uc2 Nordic Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Swedish two-year bond yields hit their lowest since late August on Wednesday at -0.516 percent.\par \par \uc2 With its crown pegged to the euro, the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would normally be expected to mimic any \uc2 ECB\uc2  rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 But Jan Storup, chief analyst at Nordea Bank, said they may have other ways to mitigate any spillover effects.\par \par \uc2 "It will put pressure on the \uc2 Danish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but won't make them cut again," he said.\par \par \uc2 "At the moment the Danish krone is stable...and if it strengthens on an \uc2 ECB\uc2  cut, they will try to use other instruments first to weaken the krone such as using \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves."\par \par \uc2 Any \uc2 ECB\uc2  stimulus may even tip the balance in Norway, where central bankers are already looking to support a weakening of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the economy adjust to lower activity in the oil industry. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/buv55s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/buv55s}}}\par \par \uc2 The Norwegian crown hit a 3-1/2 month high against the euro on Wednesday, piling pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which \uc2 Nordea\uc2  expect will cut rates by 25 basis points next year.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by John Geddie; Graphic by Nigel Stephenson; Editing by Ruth Pitchford) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-12-2T16:16:08.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151202ebc200jjk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
