\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Swiss sight deposits inch higher as fresh  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  talk surfaces\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2015\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Sight deposits only edge up despite confirmed intevention\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 UBS\uc2  economist says SNB intervion was in "homeopathic doses"\par \par \uc2 * SNB declines comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Adds \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  comment and reaction from \uc2 UBS\uc2  and \uc2 Zuercher Kantonalbank\uc2  analysts)\par \par \uc2 By Katharina Bart and Anirban Nag\par \par \uc2 ZURICH/LONDON, July 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  barely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week, data showed on Monday as fresh speculation surfaced that the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) was attempting to keep the franc down.\par \par \uc2 Sight deposits, or cash that commercial banks hold with the SNB, only inched higher last week after the SNB said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the franc's rise amid uncertainty over Greece's financial future.\par \par \uc2 Weekly deposits typically rise when the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the marginal rise last week stands in sharp contrast to rare public confirmation from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Monday that it had stepped into the market to weaken the franc.\par \par \uc2 Total sight deposits, which include other deposits on sight in Swiss francs, rose to a record 457.865 billion Swiss francs ($485.54 billion) from 456.577 billion francs in the week ending June 26.\par \par \uc2 The SNB had limited any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "only homeopathic doses" last week, said Daniel Kalt, \uc2 UBS\uc2 's chief economist for Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 The data reflect an average of sight deposits for the week, and some transactions may not be immediately visible before they are settled, which typically takes up to two days.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the overwhelming rejection by Greek voters of conditions for a rescue package from creditors on Sunday led to demand for Swiss francs, sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell to 1.0356 francs in early Pacific trading, and was last trading at 1.0448, up 0.1 percent on the day.\par \par \uc2 Dealers speculated the SNB might have been present to smoothen volatile moves in early Pacific trading when \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets opened after the Greek vote.\par \par \uc2 Traders regard the 1.03 francs level as a "line in the sand" which the SNB is keen to defend even after it dropped a cap of 1.20 francs per euro in January, and many expect it to hold for some time.\par \par \uc2 Anastassios Frangulidis, chief economist for \uc2 Zuercher Kantonalbank\uc2  in Zurich, said the SNB had shown with its unusual public comment that verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still effective.\par \par \uc2 "If they continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to what extent really depends on the next days and weeks," Frangulidis said, referring to a euro zone summit on Tuesday and encouraging signs that Greece could still reach a deal with creditors despite the referendum result.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the SNB declined to comment on potential \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ($1 = 0.9430 Swiss francs) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-7-6T09:59:14.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150706eb76008rr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
