\par\par \uc2 Foreign Exchange\par \b \uc2 Swiss  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervened \highlight\uc2  to Stabilize Franc Amid Greek Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 By John Revill   \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2015\par 13:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Global Market Stories\par \uc2 DJTGMS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 ZURICH\u8212\'20\'14\b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/moneybeat/2015/06/29/greece-markets-react-live/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the \b  \highlight22currency\b0 \highlight22  markets }}}\uc2 Sunday night to stabilize the strong franc after the concerns over Greece' potential exit from the eurozone triggered renewed buying of the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2 , Chairman of the Swiss National Bank's governing board, said the bank had been active in trying to stabilize the franc.\par \par \uc2 "It is currently a very difficult situation and we are observing developments very closely," Mr. Jordan said, referring to Greece's financial troubles and the pressure it is placing on Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an event in the Swiss capital Bern, he declined to give details about the scale of the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or whether it was the first move by the bank in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since Jan. 15, when it scrapped a cap on the franc's value.\par \par \uc2 The SNB's latest move comes amid the worsening situation in Greece, whose deepening debt crisis has edged it even closer to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/european-union-prepares-for-potential-fallout-from-greek-bank-shutdown-1435573213"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an exit from the eurozone }}}\uc2 . The country has ahead of a referendum, called to accept or reject a bailout plan by Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has imposed capital controls to prevent the country's financial system from collapse.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc, a traditional haven in times of economic or political stress, rallied in early European trading. The euro fell about 0.4% against the franc as markets opened in Asia, but has now climbed back and is trading about 0.3% lower against the franc.\par \par \uc2 At 10.09 GMT the Swiss franc was trading at 1.0399 francs per euro, after rising to 1.032 francs per euro on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Only last week Mr. Jordan said the franc remained "significantly overvalued," and said the SNB was willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary.\par \par \uc2 The latest move was in line with this policy, Mr. Jordan said on Monday. "The need was there to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mr. Jordan said.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has been dealing with the effects of a strong franc since stunning financial markets in January when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/snb-says-franc-cap-stopped-being-beneficial-1427356648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it scrapped a 3\u189\'00\'BD -year policy }}}\uc2 of capping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.20 francs per euro. The franc has risen about 13% against the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Switzerland's main trading partners since the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has already imposed negative interest rates to blunt the appeal of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier this month the SNB held a key deposit rate at -0.75%, effectively imposing a charge on deposits from commercial banks. The SNB also held its target range for the three-month London interbank offered rate, or Libor, at minus 1.25% to minus 0.25% .\par \par \uc2 The rise of franc puts pressure on Swiss exporters with the eurozone the biggest market for Swiss products like machinery, and chemicals.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the SNB's move may prove effective.\par \par \uc2 "Demand for the franc has also been limited due to SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot markets," said Stephen Gallo, a strategist at \uc2 Bank of Montreal\uc2 . Ahead of the referendum to be held in Greece next weekend, he expects the euro to remain above 1.0250 but below 1.0500 against the franc.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are reducing the attractiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a haven status. More \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to take place in the coming days, said Josh O'Byrne, analyst at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 . "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is going to continue to be volatile but the franc isn't such an attractive safe haven with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  working against you," he said.\par \par \uc2 --Chiara Albanese in London contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to John Revill at \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTGMS1120150629eb6t0008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
