\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-SNB's Jordan says will  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in market if necessary\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2015\par 18:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail)\par \par \uc2 ST. GALLEN, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 8 (Reuters) - Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is overvalued and the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary to influence monetary conditions, Swiss National Bank Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc has pared some gains in the months since the SNB's surprise policy move sent the safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soaring, amid speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the franc.\par \par \uc2 "In case there is a necessity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence monetary conditions, we will take it," Jordan told a conference in St. Gallen, Switzerland, adding the franc is "significantly overvalued".\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 15, the SNB surprised financial markets by scrapping a cap on the value of the franc against the euro it had maintained for more than three years. The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared, sparking fears for the country's export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2 Monthly foreign reserves data published on Thursday suggested the SNB may have held off on buying significant amounts of euros in April.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Alice Baghdjian; Writing by 